Huldra documentation and examples, installed in /usr/share/huldra on the
system disk (an ext2 file system on /dev/hda, mounted as the root).
Files you create anywhere on the disk survive reboots.

  docs/README.md     the project README
  examples/*.c       C programs: cc examples/hello.c -o hello && ./hello
                     or simply: cc -run examples/primes.c 1000
  scripts/hello.sh   a shell script

Software:  pkg update; pkg search; pkg install cowsay fortune 2048 sl
Network:   ifconfig; ping 10.0.2.2; wget http://host/file; httpd &
Editors:   edit FILE (Ctrl+S save, Ctrl+Q quit), less FILE, fm
Graphics:  startgui (or startgui tilewm); right-click the desktop for a menu;
           examples/window.c shows a window from C (cc -run window.c)
Games:     hack (any terminal); mines and blocks (graphical session)
Look:      a green phosphor terminal; /etc/gui.conf "crt = off" removes
           the scanlines
